2) Implementation details
- File: src/utils/branch-annotation-helpers.ts

  a) Dual-position detection and fallback (REQ-DUAL-POSITION-DETECTION, REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC, REQ-POSITION-PRIORITY)
  - gatherBranchCommentText(..):
    - Gets `beforeComments = sourceCode.getCommentsBefore(node)` and joins them into `beforeText`.
    - For `node.type === "CatchClause"`, delegates to `gatherCatchClauseCommentText(sourceCode, node, beforeText)`.

  - gatherCatchClauseCommentText(..):
    ```ts
    function gatherCatchClauseCommentText(sourceCode, node, beforeText): string {
      // Priority: if beforeText already has @story or @req, use it
      if (/@story\b/.test(beforeText) || /@req\b/.test(beforeText)) {
        return beforeText; // REQ-POSITION-PRIORITY
      }

      // Fallback 1: token-based inside comments, via getCommentsInside(node.body)
      const getCommentsInside: unknown = (sourceCode as any).getCommentsInside;
      if (node.body && typeof getCommentsInside === "function") {
        try {
          const insideComments = (getCommentsInside as (_node: any) => any[])(node.body) || [];
          const insideText = insideComments.map(extractCommentValue).join(" ");
          if (insideText) {
            return insideText; // REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC
          }
        } catch {
          // fall through to line-based fallback
        }
      }

      // Fallback 2: line-based scan of first comment-only lines inside node.body
      if (node.body && node.body.loc && node.body.loc.start && node.body.loc.end) {
        const lines = sourceCode.lines;
        const startIndex = node.body.loc.start.line - 1;
        const endIndex = node.body.loc.end.line - 1;
        const comments: string[] = [];
        let i = startIndex + 1;

        while (i <= endIndex) {
          if (!collectCommentLine(lines, i, comments)) {
            break;
          }
          i++;
        }

        const insideText = comments.join(" ");
        if (insideText) {
          return insideText; // REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC
        }
      }

      // If nothing found inside, fall back to beforeText (even if empty)
      return beforeText;
    }
    ```
  - This covers:
    • Checking before-catch comments.
    • If those don’t contain annotations, scanning inside the catch block via getCommentsInside.
    • If getCommentsInside is unavailable or empty, scanning the first comment-only lines inside the block.
    • Preferring before-catch text when it already contains @story/@req.

  b) Autofix position inside catch body (REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX)
  - getBaseBranchIndentAndInsertPos(..):
    ```ts
    if (node.type === "CatchClause" && node.body) {
      const bodyNode: any = node.body;
      const bodyStatements: any[] | undefined = Array.isArray(bodyNode.body)
        ? bodyNode.body
        : undefined;
      const firstStatement: any | undefined =
        bodyStatements && bodyStatements.length > 0
          ? bodyStatements[0]
          : undefined;

      if (firstStatement && firstStatement.loc && firstStatement.loc.start) {
        const firstLine = firstStatement.loc.start.line;
        const innerIndent =
          sourceCode.lines[firstLine - 1].match(/^(\s*)/)?.[1] || "";
        indent = innerIndent;
        insertPos = sourceCode.getIndexFromLoc({ line: firstLine, column: 0 });
      } else if (bodyNode.loc && bodyNode.loc.start) {
        const blockLine = bodyNode.loc.start.line;
        const blockIndent =
          sourceCode.lines[blockLine - 1].match(/^(\s*)/)?.[1] || "";
        const innerIndent = `${blockIndent}  `;
        indent = innerIndent;
        insertPos = sourceCode.getIndexFromLoc({ line: blockLine, column: 0 });
      }
    }
    ```
  - reportMissingStory/reportMissingReq use this indent/insertPos to insert `// @story ...` and `// @req ...`.
  - For CatchClause this results in annotations inserted as the first comment-only line inside the body, aligned with the inner indentation—precisely what Prettier will preserve.

  c) Rule integration (IMPL-BRANCH-ANNOTATION-INFO, IMPL-CATCHCLAUSE-HANDLER)
  - getBranchAnnotationInfo(..) calls gatherBranchCommentText(..) for all branch nodes—including CatchClause—so the dual-position logic is fully respected when deciding missingStory/missingReq and autofix placement.
  - src/rules/require-branch-annotation.ts uses DEFAULT_BRANCH_TYPES (which includes CatchClause) and reportMissingAnnotations on each configured branch type.

3) Tests exercising each requirement
- REQ-DUAL-POSITION-DETECTION & REQ-POSITION-PRIORITY:
  - tests/utils/branch-annotation-catch-position.test.ts
    • First test has annotations both before and inside; gatherBranchCommentText returns the before-catch annotations.

- REQ-FALLBACK-LOGIC:
  - Same file tests:
    • Inside-only comments via getCommentsInside.
    • Behavior when getCommentsInside is not available, including line-based scanning inside the block.

- REQ-PRETTIER-AUTOFIX:
  - tests/utils/branch-annotation-catch-insert-position.test.ts confirms:
    • reportMissingAnnotations inserts the fixer range at the index corresponding to the first statement in the catch body.
    • Inserted text starts with the inner indentation of that line.

- REQ-PRETTIER-COMPATIBILITY:
  - tests/integration/catch-annotation-prettier.integration.test.ts runs real Prettier + ESLint:
    • Before-catch annotations that Prettier moves inside still validate (status 0).
    • Inside-written annotations remain valid after formatting (status 0).
    • Empty catch with inside annotations passes.

- No Regression:
  - tests/rules/require-branch-annotation.test.ts continues to validate try/catch behavior and other branches (if/switch/loops) without failures.

4) Documentation
- user-docs/api-reference.md (traceability/require-branch-annotation section) explicitly documents CatchClause behavior:
  - Valid locations: immediately before `catch` OR first comment-only lines inside the catch block.
  - If annotations exist in both locations, before-catch comments take precedence.
  - Auto-fix inserts annotations inside the catch block so formatters like Prettier keep them attached.
- This matches the story’s Documentation acceptance criterion and the actual implementation.
